#12107
The Customs House~
   This small, sparsely-furnished structure serves as the local Customs House.
In earlier days, traders would stop here to detail the goods they carried in
an effort to prevent theft in their travels. However, the town is now
controlled more by pirates and merchants who frequent the port rather than
the appointed officials here. As such, the Customs House is rarely used. The
west doorway exits onto the main street.
~
