#12153
On a Beach~
   Waves lap gently at the shore of this small beach, only a quick walk from
the town of Haven. It is not used for recreation, although the waters of the
bay are both warm and sheltered. To the north, two large clay dunes provide
raw building materials, and it is for this reason the beach exists. Over time,
enough clay has been removed to create the layer of sand upon which you now
stand. Off to the west, you see the port area of Haven, which can be accessed
by a wooden boardwalk.
